---
code: K0024
title: Bad Interpolation
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, string, interpolation]
description: "String interpolation '{...}' is empty or malformed"
---

A `{...}` interpolation inside a string literal must contain exactly one valid expression. Empty braces `{}`, multiple unseparated expressions (`{ a b }`), format specifiers (`{x:.2}`), or unclosed `{` braces are syntax errors.

## Example

This error occurs when string interpolation braces are empty, contain format specifiers, or hold more than one expression:

```kura
let empty = "value: {}"
let formatted = "price: {amount:.2}"
let multi = "coords: {x y}"
```

## Solution

Place a single valid expression inside `{...}`, format numbers explicitly before interpolating, or escape literal braces with `\{` and `\}`:

```kura
let literal = "value: \{}"
let formatted = "price: {format-fixed(amount, 2)}"
let coords = "coords: {x}, {y}"
```
